# Cello Suite No. 3 in C major, BWV 1009: Bourree I and II (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a sturdy, cheerful bourree in cut time (two beats to the
# bar, quarter-note upbeat), the best known dance in the cello suites.
# Bourree II, in C minor, is quieter and more flowing (the Mutopia score
# marks it piano), and Bourree I returns da capo.
#
# Time signature: 2/2 with a quarter upbeat. Mutopia file
# cellosuite3-4.mid, the fifth score (Prelude, Allemande, Courante,
# Sarabande, Bourree): checked against cellosuite3_5_bourree.ly. The
# file holds both bourrees, 52 bars:
#   Bourree I   A 1-8, B 9-28 (each with repeat signs)
#   Bourree II  A 29-36, B 37-52 (each with repeat signs), then
#               "Bourree I da capo".
# Each half begins on the upbeat (the last quarter of the bar before).
# The MIDI plays each half once and has no da capo, so play writes out
# the traditional order: I with repeats, II with repeats, I again
# without repeats.
#
# Range: 22 notes below B2 (the low C and G, e.g. bars 4, 8, 28, 52)
# are lifted an octave by the converter.
#
# Tempo: half = 60. As performed, 132 bars of two beats, about 4:30.
# Track times: Mstislav Rostropovich (EMI, 1991) Bourree I 1:56 (56
# bars with repeats, half about 58) and Bourree II with the da capo
# 2:42 (76 bars, about 56). Confirmed from track listings. 60 is a
# touch livelier, still a dance, not a race.
#
# Structure (score bars, my reading of the Mutopia score):
#   I   A  1-8    C major, the tune, to G major (8).
#       B  9-16   G7 to C, A minor (12-16).
#          17-22  D7 and G major; falling broken chords from 21.
#          23-28  Back in C, the closing figures and cadence.
#   II  A  29-36  C minor, to E flat major (36).
#       B  37-44  E flat, G minor, D (40-44).
#          45-52  C minor colour, sequences, cadence in C minor.
#
# Bars as performed (play), numbered along the performance:
#   I  A 0.75-8.75, A repeat 8.75-16.75, B 16.75-36.75,
#      B repeat 36.75-56.75
#   II A 56.75-64.75, A repeat 64.75-72.75, B 72.75-88.75,
#      B repeat 88.75-104.75   (score x = x+28, then x+52)
#   I da capo 104.75-132.75 (score x = x+104)

pickup 4
tempo 60 2

play 0.75-8.75 0.75-8.75 8.75-28.75 8.75-28.75 28.75-36.75 28.75-36.75 36.75-52.75 36.75-52.75 0.75-28.75

dyn 1 f              # Bourree I, A first time: full
dyn 8.75 mf          # A repeat, an echo
dyn 16.75 f          # B first time
dyn 36.75 mf         # B repeat, an echo
dyn 56.75 mp         # Bourree II (piano in the score), A first time
dyn 64.75 p          # A repeat, an echo
dyn 72.75 mp         # B first time
dyn 88.75 p          # B repeat, an echo
broaden 104 0.9      # score 52: the C minor close, a breath before
                     # Bourree I returns
dyn 104.75 f         # Bourree I da capo, full, no repeats

rit 2 0.8            # the last two bars of the da capo
